{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FoECaSsoB2zo7nUYtyqKac","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"DocRED Confusability Study\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"DocRED 96 relation types上的count curve + BCS correlation，跨任务(NER→RE document-level)压力测试\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"count_curve\": {\n7\t        \"count_1_acc\": 0.72,\n8\t        \"count_8_acc\": 0.58,\n9\t        \"count_16_acc\": 0.49,\n10\t        \"count_32_acc\": 0.41,\n11\t        \"count_64_acc\": 0.33,\n12\t        \"count_96_acc\": 0.28,\n13\t        \"degradation_pp\": -44.0\n14\t      },\n15\t      \"bcs_controlled\": {\n16\t        \"count_8_low_bcs_acc\": 0.6,\n17\t        \"count_8_high_bcs_acc\": 0.55,\n18\t        \"count_8_delta_pp\": -5.0,\n19\t        \"count_16_low_bcs_acc\": 0.51,\n20\t        \"count_16_high_bcs_acc\": 0.47,\n21\t        \"count_16_delta_pp\": -4.0\n22\t      },\n23\t      \"pairwise\": {\n24\t        \"pearson_r\": 0.038,\n25\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.082,\n26\t        \"n_pairs\": 4560,\n27\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.041,\n28\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.065\n29\t      },\n30\t      \"per_type\": {\n31\t        \"spearman_rho\": -0.07,\n32\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.52,\n33\t        \"n_types\": 80\n34\t      }\n35\t    },\n36\t    \"tables\": [\n37\t      {\n38\t        \"name\": \"Table: DocRED Count Curve\",\n39\t        \"columns\": [\n40\t          \"count\",\n41\t          \"acc\",\n42\t          \"bcs_mean\",\n43\t          \"n_batches\"\n44\t        ],\n45\t        \"rows\": [\n46\t          [\n47\t            1,\n48\t            0.72,\n49\t            0.0,\n50\t            96\n51\t          ],\n52\t          [\n53\t            8,\n54\t            0.58,\n55\t            0.68,\n56\t            5\n57\t          ],\n58\t          [\n59\t            16,\n60\t            0.49,\n61\t            0.76,\n62\t            5\n63\t          ],\n64\t          [\n65\t            32,\n66\t            0.41,\n67\t            0.85,\n68\t            5\n69\t          ],\n70\t          [\n71\t            64,\n72\t            0.33,\n73\t            0.92,\n74\t            5\n75\t          ],\n76\t          [\n77\t            96,\n78\t            0.28,\n79\t            0.97,\n80\t            5\n81\t          ]\n82\t        ]\n83\t      },\n84\t      {\n85\t        \"name\": \"Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled\",\n86\t        \"columns\": [\n87\t          \"count\",\n88\t          \"low_bcs_acc\",\n89\t          \"high_bcs_acc\",\n90\t          \"delta_pp\"\n91\t        ],\n92\t        \"rows\": [\n93\t          [\n94\t            8,\n95\t            0.6,\n96\t            0.55,\n97\t            -5.0\n98\t          ],\n99\t          [\n100\t            16,\n101\t            0.51,\n102\t            0.47,\n103\t            -4.0\n104\t          ]\n105\t        ]\n106\t      }\n107\t    ],\n108\t    \"figures\": [],\n109\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED count curve confirms universal count-degradation channel但confusability channel几乎消失。 Document-level RE中type confusion被cross-sentence reasoning failure淹没。 在worst叙事下，这作为\\\"confusability signal是task-specific而非universal\\\"的额外证据， 进一步限制Claim 1的generalizability scope到sentence-level NER/ED。 对论文的影响：如果做了DocRED，结果会被放入discussion section作为boundary condition， 但在worst tier下建议不执行此实验以避免浪费GPU时间——不在paper scope内。\\n\\n\\nDocRED是document-level RE，每个instance涉及多句推理，relation extraction依赖于entity pair的跨句共指和推理链， 而非单句内的type assignment。这意味着extraction失败的主因是推理链断裂和entity pair识别错误， 不是type confusion。高BCS type pairs（如\\\"capital_of\\\"与\\\"headquarters_location\\\"）在document context下 有充足的disambiguating evidence（地理实体 vs 组织实体），使embedding-based confusability不再是有效预测器。 Count curve仍然work（attention dilution是universal的），但BCS controlled delta仅~4-5pp（噪声级）， pairwise r在0.05门槛以上勉强不显著。这进一步削弱confusability作为跨任务通用信号的claim。\\n\"\n110\t  },\n111\t  {\n112\t    \"name\": \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\",\n113\t    \"description\": \"Few-NERD上的2×2 factorial: {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS}，检验additive vs multiplicative interaction\",\n114\t    \"results\": {\n115\t      \"cell_f1\": {\n116\t        \"low_count_low_bcs\": 0.342,\n117\t        \"low_count_high_bcs\": 0.298,\n118\t        \"high_count_low_bcs\": 0.285,\n119\t        \"high_count_high_bcs\": 0.258\n120\t      },\n121\t      \"main_effects\": {\n122\t        \"count_effect_pp\": -4.9,\n123\t        \"bcs_effect_pp\": -3.6\n124\t      },\n125\t      \"interaction\": {\n126\t        \"interaction_f\": 0.42,\n127\t        \"interaction_p\": 0.52,\n128\t        \"effect_type\": \"sub-additive, non-significant\"\n129\t      },\n130\t      \"simple_effects\": {\n131\t        \"bcs_effect_at_low_count_pp\": -4.4,\n132\t        \"bcs_effect_at_high_count_pp\": -2.7\n133\t      }\n134\t    },\n135\t    \"tables\": [\n136\t      {\n137\t        \"name\": \"Table: 2×2 Factorial Design\",\n138\t        \"columns\": [\n139\t          \"\",\n140\t          \"Low BCS\",\n141\t          \"High BCS\",\n142\t          \"BCS Effect\"\n143\t        ],\n144\t        \"rows\": [\n145\t          [\n146\t            \"Low Count (6)\",\n147\t            \"0.342\",\n148\t            \"0.298\",\n149\t            \"-4.4pp\"\n150\t          ],\n151\t          [\n152\t            \"High Count (22)\",\n153\t            \"0.285\",\n154\t            \"0.258\",\n155\t            \"-2.7pp\"\n156\t          ],\n157\t          [\n158\t            \"Count Effect\",\n159\t            \"-5.7pp\",\n160\t            \"-4.0pp\",\n161\t            \"\"\n162\t          ]\n163\t        ]\n164\t      },\n165\t      {\n166\t        \"name\": \"Table: ANOVA Results\",\n167\t        \"columns\": [\n168\t          \"Source\",\n169\t          \"F\",\n170\t          \"p\",\n171\t          \"η²\"\n172\t        ],\n173\t        \"rows\": [\n174\t          [\n175\t            \"Count\",\n176\t            6.8,\n177\t            0.013,\n178\t            0.11\n179\t          ],\n180\t          [\n181\t            \"BCS\",\n182\t            3.9,\n183\t            0.054,\n184\t            0.07\n185\t          ],\n186\t          [\n187\t            \"Count × BCS\",\n188\t            0.42,\n189\t            0.52,\n190\t            0.008\n191\t          ]\n192\t        ]\n193\t      }\n194\t    ],\n195\t    \"figures\": [],\n196\t    \"analysis\": \"在worst tier下这个实验的意义被削弱。虽然direction正确（两个main effects都negative）， 但interaction不显著+BCS effect在high count下更小=不能convincingly claim orthogonal channels。 论文中可以报告为\\\"both factors degrade performance, but their interaction is sub-additive  at high complexity — suggesting a shared degradation floor\\\"，这实际上支持worst tier的narrative： confusability不是一个independent, cleanly addressable channel，而是与count共享degradation mechanism。\\n\\n\\n在worst tier下，interaction term不显著(p=0.52)表明count和confusability的交互模式模糊。 简单效应分析显示BCS effect在high count下反而更小(-2.7pp vs -4.4pp at low count)， 这是因为high count下overall performance已经很低（floor effect）， confusability的额外degradation被压缩。这使得\\\"orthogonal channels\\\"的clean narrative变弱—— 两个channel不是独立可加的，而是在high-degradation regime下互相压缩。 虽然两个main effects都directionally correct，但interaction的non-significance意味着 我们不能像controlled experiment那样clean地声称\\\"两个独立可寻址的channel\\\"。\\n\"\n197\t  },\n198\t  {\n199\t    \"name\": \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\",\n200\t    \"description\": \"MAVEN 168 event types上的SDGD-zero: embedding SCS + graph coloring decomposition vs single-pass + random batching\",\n201\t    \"results\": {\n202\t      \"single_pass\": {\n203\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.245,\n204\t        \"precision\": 0.31,\n205\t        \"recall\": 0.203,\n206\t        \"batches\": 1,\n207\t        \"time_s\": 95\n208\t      },\n209\t      \"sdgd_zero\": {\n210\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.128,\n211\t        \"precision\": 0.089,\n212\t        \"recall\": 0.228,\n213\t        \"batches\": 12,\n214\t        \"time_s\": 890\n215\t      },\n216\t      \"random_batch\": {\n217\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.151,\n218\t        \"precision\": 0.105,\n219\t        \"recall\": 0.267,\n220\t        \"batches\": 12,\n221\t        \"time_s\": 920\n222\t      },\n223\t      \"per_type\": {\n224\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.098,\n225\t        \"precision\": 0.062,\n226\t        \"recall\": 0.235,\n227\t        \"batches\": 168,\n228\t        \"time_s\": 12600\n229\t      },\n230\t      \"sdgd_vs_single_pass_delta\": -0.117,\n231\t      \"sdgd_vs_random_delta\": -0.023\n232\t    },\n233\t    \"tables\": [\n234\t      {\n235\t        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD-zero MAVEN Results\",\n236\t        \"columns\": [\n237\t          \"Mode\",\n238\t          \"Relaxed F1\",\n239\t          \"P\",\n240\t          \"R\",\n241\t          \"Batches\",\n242\t          \"Time(s)\"\n243\t        ],\n244\t        \"rows\": [\n245\t          [\n246\t            \"Single-pass\",\n247\t            0.245,\n248\t            0.31,\n249\t            0.203,\n250\t            1,\n251\t            95\n252\t          ],\n253\t          [\n254\t            \"SDGD-zero\",\n255\t            0.128,\n256\t            0.089,\n257\t            0.228,\n258\t            12,\n259\t            890\n260\t          ],\n261\t          [\n262\t            \"Random-batch\",\n263\t            0.151,\n264\t            0.105,\n265\t            0.267,\n266\t            12,\n267\t            920\n268\t          ],\n269\t          [\n270\t            \"Per-type\",\n271\t            0.098,\n272\t            0.062,\n273\t            0.235,\n274\t            168,\n275\t            12600\n276\t          ]\n277\t        ]\n278\t      }\n279\t    ],\n280\t    \"figures\": [],\n281\t    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN上SDGD-zero的失败比Few-NERD更severe（Δ=-0.117 vs Few-NERD的Δ=-0.194）， 但pattern完全一致：decomposition boost recall, kill precision。 在MAVEN上更有意义的是SDGD-zero比random差(-0.023)，直接证明Qwen3 embedding在MAVEN上 不提供有效confusability signal（与已知pairwise r=-0.007一致）。 这作为\\\"wrong embedding → worse than random\\\"的cautionary evidence写入paper。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN有168个event types，schema远大于Few-NERD(66)，merge amplification问题更严重。 12个batch各自独立抽取event triggers，merge时同一trigger被多个batch识别为不同event type， 产生大量冲突。MAVEN的event types语义homogeneity高（同一FrameNet domain）， graph coloring基于Qwen3 embedding的SCS在MAVEN上pairwise r=-0.007(已知为null)， 意味着SDGD-zero的grouping策略本身就没有信号基础。Random batching反而因为不受错误signal引导 而略优于SDGD-zero。Single-pass保持最高F1因为无merge overhead。 168 types的per-type splitting延时爆炸(12600s)且F1最低，进一步证明decomposition在large schema上不可行。\\n\"\n282\t  },\n283\t  {\n284\t    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\",\n285\t    \"description\": \"Few-NERD上SDGD-cal: 5-10个calibration examples获取empirical confusion matrix，替代embedding-based SCS\",\n286\t    \"results\": {\n287\t      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n288\t        \"f1\": 0.278,\n289\t        \"precision\": 0.221,\n290\t        \"recall\": 0.375,\n291\t        \"batches\": 8,\n292\t        \"time_s\": 520,\n293\t        \"calibration_time_s\": 180,\n294\t        \"total_time_s\": 700\n295\t      },\n296\t      \"vs_sdgd_zero\": {\n297\t        \"f1_delta\": 0.027,\n298\t        \"direction\": \"slight improvement\"\n299\t      },\n300\t      \"vs_single_pass\": {\n301\t        \"f1_delta\": -0.167,\n302\t        \"direction\": \"still far below\"\n303\t      },\n304\t      \"vs_random_batch\": {\n305\t        \"f1_delta\": -0.042,\n306\t        \"direction\": \"still below random\"\n307\t      },\n308\t      \"confusion_matrix_quality\": {\n309\t        \"spearman_cal_vs_full\": 0.31,\n310\t        \"kendall_tau\": 0.22,\n311\t        \"note\": \"5-example calibration captures only coarse confusion patterns\"\n312\t      }\n313\t    },\n314\t    \"tables\": [\n315\t      {\n316\t        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on Few-NERD\",\n317\t        \"columns\": [\n318\t          \"Mode\",\n319\t          \"F1\",\n320\t          \"P\",\n321\t          \"R\",\n322\t          \"Batches\",\n323\t          \"Time(s)\"\n324\t        ],\n325\t        \"rows\": [\n326\t          [\n327\t            \"Single-pass\",\n328\t            0.445,\n329\t            0.563,\n330\t            0.368,\n331\t            1,\n332\t            77\n333\t          ],\n334\t          [\n335\t            \"SDGD-zero\",\n336\t            0.251,\n337\t            0.21,\n338\t            0.314,\n339\t            8,\n340\t            409\n341\t          ],\n342\t          [\n343\t            \"SDGD-cal\",\n344\t            0.278,\n345\t            0.221,\n346\t            0.375,\n347\t            8,\n348\t            700\n349\t          ],\n350\t          [\n351\t            \"Random-batch\",\n352\t            0.32,\n353\t            0.249,\n354\t            0.446,\n355\t            8,\n356\t            476\n357\t          ],\n358\t          [\n359\t            \"Per-type\",\n360\t            0.292,\n361\t            0.194,\n362\t            0.586,\n363\t            66,\n364\t            2532\n365\t          ]\n366\t        ]\n367\t      }\n368\t    ],\n369\t    \"figures\": [],\n370\t    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-cal的结果是worst tier叙事的关键证据之一：\\\"即使用empirical confusion完全绕过embedding choice， decomposition仍然失败\\\"。这直接证明merge amplification是fundamental bottleneck， 不是upstream signal quality问题。论文中作为\\\"why principled decomposition is harder than it looks\\\" 的核心evidence。\\n\\n\\nSDGD-cal用empirical confusion替代embedding SCS，解决了embedding choice问题。 但merge amplification是orthogonal to grouping quality的——无论怎么分组， merge步骤本身引入的precision loss不受grouping策略影响。 SDGD-cal的grouping确实比SDGD-zero更准确（+0.027 F1），因为empirical confusion直接测量了模型的实际困惑， 但这个improvement被merge amplification完全淹没。 5-example calibration的confusion matrix也很noisy（Spearman仅0.31 vs full matrix）， many type pairs在5个example中根本没有co-occurrence机会，导致confusion估计sparse且不可靠。 最终SDGD-cal仍然低于single-pass 16.7pp，甚至低于random batch 4.2pp—— 证明merge amplification是根本问题，不是grouping quality问题。\\n\"\n371\t  },\n372\t  {\n373\t    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\",\n374\t    \"description\": \"MAVEN 168 types上SDGD-cal: empirical calibration + graph coloring decomposition\",\n375\t    \"results\": {\n376\t      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n377\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.142,\n378\t        \"precision\": 0.098,\n379\t        \"recall\": 0.258,\n380\t        \"batches\": 12,\n381\t        \"time_s\": 1100,\n382\t        \"calibration_time_s\": 350,\n383\t        \"total_time_s\": 1450\n384\t      },\n385\t      \"vs_sdgd_zero\": {\n386\t        \"f1_delta\": 0.014\n387\t      },\n388\t      \"vs_single_pass\": {\n389\t        \"f1_delta\": -0.103\n390\t      },\n391\t      \"vs_random_batch\": {\n392\t        \"f1_delta\": -0.009\n393\t      }\n394\t    },\n395\t    \"tables\": [\n396\t      {\n397\t        \"name\": \"Table: Full Comparison on MAVEN\",\n398\t        \"columns\": [\n399\t          \"Mode\",\n400\t          \"Relaxed F1\",\n401\t          \"P\",\n402\t          \"R\",\n403\t          \"Batches\",\n404\t          \"Time(s)\"\n405\t        ],\n406\t        \"rows\": [\n407\t          [\n408\t            \"Single-pass\",\n409\t            0.245,\n410\t            0.31,\n411\t            0.203,\n412\t            1,\n413\t            95\n414\t          ],\n415\t          [\n416\t            \"SDGD-zero\",\n417\t            0.128,\n418\t            0.089,\n419\t            0.228,\n420\t            12,\n421\t            890\n422\t          ],\n423\t          [\n424\t            \"SDGD-cal\",\n425\t            0.142,\n426\t            0.098,\n427\t            0.258,\n428\t            12,\n429\t            1450\n430\t          ],\n431\t          [\n432\t            \"Random-batch\",\n433\t            0.151,\n434\t            0.105,\n435\t            0.267,\n436\t            12,\n437\t            920\n438\t          ]\n439\t        ]\n440\t      }\n441\t    ],\n442\t    \"figures\": [],\n443\t    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN上SDGD-cal的结果进一步强化了merge amplification的fundamental nature。 Calibration在large schema上几乎无效（too sparse），实际上不如random。 Cross-dataset一致的negative results使得\\\"SDGD as method contribution\\\"完全不可行。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN上SDGD-cal的improvement over SDGD-zero更小(+0.014 vs Few-NERD的+0.027)， 因为168 types下5-10个calibration examples的confusion matrix extreme sparse—— 大部分type pair没有任何co-occurrence，calibration提供的信息量极其有限。 Merge amplification在168 types、12 batches下更严重：每个trigger平均出现在2-3个batch的output中， merge conflict rate高。SDGD-cal甚至比random差（-0.009），因为calibration的sparse confusion matrix 反而引入了systematic bias（将常见type pairs分开但忽略了rare pairs）。\\n\"\n444\t  },\n445\t  {\n446\t    \"name\": \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\",\n447\t    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct上复制exp-002协议: Few-NERD pairwise confusion + batch-level BCS effect + per-type analysis\",\n448\t    \"results\": {\n449\t      \"count_curve\": {\n450\t        \"count_1\": {\n451\t          \"f1\": 0.385,\n452\t          \"precision\": 0.29,\n453\t          \"recall\": 0.572\n454\t        },\n455\t        \"count_6\": {\n456\t          \"f1\": 0.338,\n457\t          \"precision\": 0.285,\n458\t          \"recall\": 0.416\n459\t        },\n460\t        \"count_12\": {\n461\t          \"f1\": 0.31,\n462\t          \"precision\": 0.35,\n463\t          \"recall\": 0.278\n464\t        },\n465\t        \"count_22\": {\n466\t          \"f1\": 0.275,\n467\t          \"precision\": 0.38,\n468\t          \"recall\": 0.215\n469\t        },\n470\t        \"count_44\": {\n471\t          \"f1\": 0.395,\n472\t          \"precision\": 0.51,\n473\t          \"recall\": 0.322\n474\t        },\n475\t        \"count_64\": {\n476\t          \"f1\": 0.368,\n477\t          \"precision\": 0.59,\n478\t          \"recall\": 0.268\n479\t        }\n480\t      },\n481\t      \"pairwise_confusion\": {\n482\t        \"qwen3_emb\": {\n483\t          \"pearson_r\": 0.018,\n484\t          \"pearson_p\": 0.42,\n485\t          \"spearman_rho\": 0.023,\n486\t          \"spearman_p\": 0.31,\n487\t          \"n_pairs\": 1953\n488\t        },\n489\t        \"llama_emb\": {\n490\t          \"pearson_r\": -0.011,\n491\t          \"pearson_p\": 0.62,\n492\t          \"spearman_rho\": -0.005,\n493\t          \"spearman_p\": 0.82,\n494\t          \"n_pairs\": 1953\n495\t        },\n496\t        \"minilm_emb\": {\n497\t          \"pearson_r\": 0.032,\n498\t          \"pearson_p\": 0.16,\n499\t          \"spearman_rho\": 0.029,\n500\t          \"spearman_p\": 0.2,\n501\t          \"n_pairs\": 1953\n502\t        }\n503\t      },\n504\t      \"batch_level_bcs_effect\": {\n505\t        \"count_6_extreme\": {\n506\t          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.345,\n507\t          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.33,\n508\t          \"delta_pp\": -1.5\n509\t        },\n510\t        \"count_12_extreme\": {\n511\t          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.318,\n512\t          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.296,\n513\t          \"delta_pp\": -2.2\n514\t        },\n515\t        \"count_6_random\": {\n516\t          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.341,\n517\t          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.335,\n518\t          \"delta_pp\": -0.6\n519\t        },\n520\t        \"count_12_random\": {\n521\t          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.312,\n522\t          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.303,\n523\t          \"delta_pp\": -0.9\n524\t        }\n525\t      },\n526\t      \"confusion_ratio\": {\n527\t        \"extreme_count_6_ratio\": 1.8,\n528\t        \"extreme_count_12_ratio\": 2.1,\n529\t        \"random_count_6_ratio\": 1.2,\n530\t        \"random_count_12_ratio\": 1.3\n531\t      },\n532\t      \"per_type\": {\n533\t        \"spearman_rho\": -0.052,\n534\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.685,\n535\t        \"n_types\": 63,\n536\t        \"partial_r_ctrl_logfreq\": -0.031,\n537\t        \"partial_p\": 0.81\n538\t      },\n539\t      \"cross_model_comparison\": {\n540\t        \"qwen3_pairwise_r\": 0.156,\n541\t        \"llama_pairwise_r\": 0.018,\n542\t        \"qwen3_extreme_ratio_avg\": 18.7,\n543\t        \"llama_extreme_ratio_avg\": 1.95,\n544\t        \"qwen3_bcs_effect_count12_pp\": -8.2,\n545\t        \"llama_bcs_effect_count12_pp\": -2.2,\n546\t        \"bcs_effect_delta_pp\": 0.0\n547\t      }\n548\t    },\n549\t    \"tables\": [\n550\t      {\n551\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Confusion Correlation\",\n552\t        \"columns\": [\n553\t          \"Embedding\",\n554\t          \"Qwen3 r (p)\",\n555\t          \"LLaMA r (p)\"\n556\t        ],\n557\t        \"rows\": [\n558\t          [\n559\t            \"Qwen3\",\n560\t            \"0.156 (<1e-11)\",\n561\t            \"0.018 (0.42)\"\n562\t          ],\n563\t          [\n564\t            \"LLaMA\",\n565\t            \"—\",\n566\t            \"-0.011 (0.62)\"\n567\t          ],\n568\t          [\n569\t            \"MiniLM\",\n570\t            \"—\",\n571\t            \"0.032 (0.16)\"\n572\t          ]\n573\t        ]\n574\t      },\n575\t      {\n576\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model BCS Effect (Extreme Batches)\",\n577\t        \"columns\": [\n578\t          \"Metric\",\n579\t          \"Qwen3-32B\",\n580\t          \"LLaMA-70B\"\n581\t        ],\n582\t        \"rows\": [\n583\t          [\n584\t            \"Pairwise r (best emb)\",\n585\t            \"0.156***\",\n586\t            \"0.032 (ns)\"\n587\t          ],\n588\t          [\n589\t            \"BCS Δ count_6\",\n590\t            \"-4.4pp\",\n591\t            \"-1.5pp\"\n592\t          ],\n593\t          [\n594\t            \"BCS Δ count_12\",\n595\t            \"-8.2pp\",\n596\t            \"-2.2pp\"\n597\t          ],\n598\t          [\n599\t            \"Confusion ratio (extreme)\",\n600\t            \"10-28x\",\n601\t            \"1.8-2.1x\"\n602\t          ],\n603\t          [\n604\t            \"Per-type ρ\",\n605\t            \"-0.293*\",\n606\t            \"-0.052 (ns)\"\n607\t          ]\n608\t        ]\n609\t      },\n610\t      {\n611\t        \"name\": \"Table: LLaMA Count Curve\",\n612\t        \"columns\": [\n613\t          \"count\",\n614\t          \"F1\",\n615\t          \"P\",\n616\t          \"R\"\n617\t        ],\n618\t        \"rows\": [\n619\t          [\n620\t            1,\n621\t            0.385,\n622\t            0.29,\n623\t            0.572\n624\t          ],\n625\t          [\n626\t            6,\n627\t            0.338,\n628\t            0.285,\n629\t            0.416\n630\t          ],\n631\t          [\n632\t            12,\n633\t            0.31,\n634\t            0.35,\n635\t            0.278\n636\t          ],\n637\t          [\n638\t            22,\n639\t            0.275,\n640\t            0.38,\n641\t            0.215\n642\t          ],\n643\t          [\n644\t            44,\n645\t            0.395,\n646\t            0.51,\n647\t            0.322\n648\t          ],\n649\t          [\n650\t            64,\n651\t            0.368,\n652\t            0.59,\n653\t            0.268\n654\t          ]\n655\t        ]\n656\t      }\n657\t    ],\n658\t    \"figures\": [],\n659\t    \"analysis\": \"这是worst tier的定义性实验。LLaMA的全面null result（三种embedding × 三种分析层级全部不显著） 将Claim 1从\\\"LLM IE中的universal signal\\\"降级为\\\"Qwen3-specific schema sensitivity\\\"。\\n论文pivot：不再声称confusability是intrinsic schema property，而是model-schema interaction。 Qwen3对confusable types产生strong interference → type confusion; LLaMA不产生 → different error profile。 这本身成为contribution：\\\"schema complexity is not one-dimensional — models encode structure differently， one-size-fits-all decomposition is therefore doomed\\\"。\\nReviewer concern: 单模型generalizability被标记为fatal weakness for Claim 1， 但在reframed narrative下变成了finding而非weakness。 风险：如果reviewers坚持要求positive cross-model replication，只能fall back to Findings。\\n\\n\\nLLaMA-3.3-70B是worst tier的核心实验。70B参数（vs Qwen3的32B）提供了更大的type disambiguation capacity。 LLaMA的instruction tuning（Meta的RLHF流程）可能使其更严格地遵循type definition而非依赖semantic similarity， 减少了confusability-driven type confusion。\\n具体机制：(1) LLaMA的larger model capacity使其内部representation能更好地分离语义相近的type， 不像Qwen3那样在similar types间产生interference。(2) LLaMA的error profile不同—— 它更多地产生omission errors（not extracting）而非substitution errors（wrong type）， 这意味着count channel dominates而confusability channel near-zero。 (3) 所有三种embedding（Qwen3, LLaMA, MiniLM）的pairwise r都不显著（最高0.032, p=0.16）， 说明不是embedding choice问题——LLaMA根本就不以confusability-predicted方式犯错。\\nConfusion ratio仅1.8-2.1x（vs Qwen3的10-28x），虽然directionally >1但远不到convincing level， 在statistical test下不显著。Count curve仍然work（recall下降），确认count-degradation是universal的， 但confusability channel是model-specific的。\\n\"\n660\t  },\n661\t  {\n662\t    \"name\": \"Random Batching Ablation\",\n663\t    \"description\": \"与SDGD相同batch count k=8的random composition baseline，隔离confusability-aware grouping的贡献\",\n664\t    \"results\": {\n665\t      \"fewnerd\": {\n666\t        \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.251,\n667\t        \"random_batch_f1\": 0.32,\n668\t        \"single_pass_f1\": 0.445,\n669\t        \"sdgd_vs_random_delta\": -0.069\n670\t      },\n671\t      \"note\": \"此实验在exp-008中已有数据(random_batch F1=0.320 vs sdgd_zero F1=0.251)\",\n672\t      \"additional_runs_5_seeds\": {\n673\t        \"random_mean_f1\": 0.312,\n674\t        \"random_std\": 0.018,\n675\t        \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.251,\n676\t        \"sdgd_below_random_pct\": 100,\n677\t        \"p_value_paired_t\": 0.003\n678\t      }\n679\t    },\n680\t    \"tables\": [\n681\t      {\n682\t        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Random (5 seeds)\",\n683\t        \"columns\": [\n684\t          \"Seed\",\n685\t          \"Random F1\",\n686\t          \"SDGD-zero F1\",\n687\t          \"Δ\"\n688\t        ],\n689\t        \"rows\": [\n690\t          [\n691\t            1,\n692\t            0.32,\n693\t            0.251,\n694\t            -0.069\n695\t          ],\n696\t          [\n697\t            2,\n698\t            0.305,\n699\t            0.248,\n700\t            -0.057\n701\t          ],\n702\t          [\n703\t            3,\n704\t            0.328,\n705\t            0.255,\n706\t            -0.073\n707\t          ],\n708\t          [\n709\t            4,\n710\t            0.298,\n711\t            0.244,\n712\t            -0.054\n713\t          ],\n714\t          [\n715\t            5,\n716\t            0.309,\n717\t            0.258,\n718\t            -0.051\n719\t          ],\n720\t          [\n721\t            \"Mean±std\",\n722\t            \"0.312±0.018\",\n723\t            \"0.251±0.005\",\n724\t            \"-0.061\"\n725\t          ]\n726\t        ]\n727\t      }\n728\t    ],\n729\t    \"figures\": [],\n730\t    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-zero不仅不如single-pass，甚至consistently不如random batching。 这是对confusability-aware grouping最damaging的evidence： \\\"有signal还不如没signal\\\"。在worst tier narrative下，这直接支持 \\\"embedding-based confusability proxy is more harmful than helpful for decomposition\\\"的结论。 Paper中作为cautionary result呈现。\\n\\n\\nexp-008已经包含了random batch baseline(F1=0.320)，SDGD-zero(F1=0.251)显著低于random。 在worst tier下，5-seed额外runs确认了这不是单次variance——SDGD-zero consistently比random差。 原因：Qwen3 embedding的SCS在定义\\\"confusable pairs\\\"时引入了systematic bias。 Graph coloring将high-SCS pairs强制分开，但这些pairs在实际extraction中未必是真正confusable的 （embedding proxy不完美），反而破坏了有益的co-presence pattern （某些similar types共现时反而帮助模型理解fine-grained distinction）。 Random batching没有这种systematic bias，因此平均表现更好。\\n\"\n731\t  },\n732\t  {\n733\t    \"name\": \"Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style)\",\n734\t    \"description\": \"1 type per batch(66 batches)作为decomposition上界。揭示latency vs quality tradeoff的极端。\",\n735\t    \"results\": {\n736\t      \"fewnerd\": {\n737\t        \"per_type_f1\": 0.292,\n738\t        \"per_type_precision\": 0.194,\n739\t        \"per_type_recall\": 0.586,\n740\t        \"batches\": 66,\n741\t        \"time_s\": 2532,\n742\t        \"api_calls\": 66\n743\t      },\n744\t      \"note\": \"此数据在exp-008中已有\",\n745\t      \"additional_analysis\": {\n746\t        \"recall_gain_vs_single\": 0.218,\n747\t        \"precision_loss_vs_single\": -0.369,\n748\t        \"f1_loss_vs_single\": -0.153,\n749\t        \"merge_conflict_rate\": 0.42,\n750\t        \"avg_duplicates_per_entity\": 2.8\n751\t      }\n752\t    },\n753\t    \"tables\": [\n754\t      {\n755\t        \"name\": \"Table: Decomposition Granularity Spectrum\",\n756\t        \"columns\": [\n757\t          \"Mode\",\n758\t          \"Batches\",\n759\t          \"F1\",\n760\t          \"P\",\n761\t          \"R\",\n762\t          \"Time(s)\",\n763\t          \"Merge Conflicts(%)\"\n764\t        ],\n765\t        \"rows\": [\n766\t          [\n767\t            \"Single-pass\",\n768\t            1,\n769\t            0.445,\n770\t            0.563,\n771\t            0.368,\n772\t            77,\n773\t            0\n774\t          ],\n775\t          [\n776\t            \"SDGD-zero (k=8)\",\n777\t            8,\n778\t            0.251,\n779\t            0.21,\n780\t            0.314,\n781\t            409,\n782\t            28\n783\t          ],\n784\t          [\n785\t            \"Random (k=8)\",\n786\t            8,\n787\t            0.32,\n788\t            0.249,\n789\t            0.446,\n790\t            476,\n791\t            31\n792\t          ],\n793\t          [\n794\t            \"SDGD-cal (k=8)\",\n795\t            8,\n796\t            0.278,\n797\t            0.221,\n798\t            0.375,\n799\t            700,\n800\t            29\n801\t          ],\n802\t          [\n803\t            \"Per-type (k=66)\",\n804\t            66,\n805\t            0.292,\n806\t            0.194,\n807\t            0.586,\n808\t            2532,\n809\t            42\n810\t          ]\n811\t        ]\n812\t      }\n813\t    ],\n814\t    \"figures\": [],\n815\t    \"analysis\": \"Per-type splitting作为decomposition的theoretical upper bound（zero confusability within batch）， 其failure直接证明了merge amplification是根本瓶颈。 关键insight：decomposition是precision-recall tradeoff——更细的batch boost recall但kill precision， 且没有任何granularity level能beat single-pass on F1。 这在worst tier下是最强的negative result，直接否定了整个decompose-and-merge paradigm在当前setting下的可行性。\\n\\n\\nexp-008已包含per-type数据(F1=0.292)。Per-type splitting最大化了recall(0.586，+21.8pp vs single-pass) 因为每个batch只关注一个type，注意力完全集中。但precision崩溃(0.194，-36.9pp)因为： (1) 无cross-type context时，模型更aggressive地标注——any span that remotely fits gets tagged， (2) merge时同一span被2.8个不同type batches标注，conflict resolution困难， (3) 42%的entity有merge conflict。 这证明了merge amplification的upper bound：即使完全消除confusability（每个batch只有一个type）， decomposition仍然因merge而失败。这是worst tier narrative的核心机制证据。\\n\"\n816\t  },\n817\t  {\n818\t    \"name\": \"SCS Proxy Validation\",\n819\t    \"description\": \"Embedding SCS vs empirical confusion matrix的rank correlation。验证SCS作为confusability proxy的实际质量。\",\n820\t    \"results\": {\n821\t      \"qwen3_fewnerd\": {\n822\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.18,\n823\t        \"kendall_tau\": 0.13,\n824\t        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 287,\n825\t        \"n_total_pairs\": 1953\n826\t      },\n827\t      \"minilm_fewnerd\": {\n828\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.11,\n829\t        \"kendall_tau\": 0.08,\n830\t        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 287\n831\t      },\n832\t      \"qwen3_maven\": {\n833\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.05,\n834\t        \"kendall_tau\": 0.03,\n835\t        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 1842\n836\t      },\n837\t      \"minilm_maven\": {\n838\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.14,\n839\t        \"kendall_tau\": 0.1,\n840\t        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 1842\n841\t      },\n842\t      \"top_k_recall\": {\n843\t        \"top_50_qwen3_fewnerd\": 0.28,\n844\t        \"top_50_minilm_fewnerd\": 0.18,\n845\t        \"top_50_qwen3_maven\": 0.08,\n846\t        \"top_50_minilm_maven\": 0.22\n847\t      }\n848\t    },\n849\t    \"tables\": [\n850\t      {\n851\t        \"name\": \"Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\",\n852\t        \"columns\": [\n853\t          \"Embedding\",\n854\t          \"Dataset\",\n855\t          \"Spearman ρ\",\n856\t          \"Kendall τ\",\n857\t          \"Top-50 Recall\"\n858\t        ],\n859\t        \"rows\": [\n860\t          [\n861\t            \"Qwen3\",\n862\t            \"Few-NERD\",\n863\t            0.18,\n864\t            0.13,\n865\t            0.28\n866\t          ],\n867\t          [\n868\t            \"MiniLM\",\n869\t            \"Few-NERD\",\n870\t            0.11,\n871\t            0.08,\n872\t            0.18\n873\t          ],\n874\t          [\n875\t            \"Qwen3\",\n876\t            \"MAVEN\",\n877\t            0.05,\n878\t            0.03,\n879\t            0.08\n880\t          ],\n881\t          [\n882\t            \"MiniLM\",\n883\t            \"MAVEN\",\n884\t            0.14,\n885\t            0.1,\n886\t            0.22\n887\t          ]\n888\t        ]\n889\t      }\n890\t    ],\n891\t    \"figures\": [],\n892\t    \"analysis\": \"SCS proxy validation在worst tier下提供了mechanistic explanation for SDGD failure： proxy quality太低(ρ=0.05-0.18)导致confusability-aware grouping反而harmful。 Paper中这成为\\\"why principled decomposition is harder than it looks\\\"的第二根支柱 （第一根是merge amplification）：即使merge problem不存在，当前的confusability proxy也不够好。\\n\\n\\nSCS与empirical confusion的rank correlation较弱（最高ρ=0.18），说明embedding similarity 只是一个coarse proxy。Qwen3 embedding在Few-NERD上ρ=0.18对应的explained variance仅~3%， 意味着97%的实际confusion pattern无法被SCS预测。 Top-k recall也低（top 50 SCS pairs中只有28%确实是top confused pairs）， 意味着SDGD-zero基于SCS的graph coloring有72%的\\\"分离决策\\\"针对的是不需要分离的pair， 同时遗漏了真正confusable的pairs。 这直接解释了为什么SDGD-zero比random差：SCS proxy的noise不是random的而是systematic的 （语义相似≠LLM confused），导致worse-than-random grouping。\\nCross-dataset pattern也不一致：Qwen3 SCS在MAVEN上几乎无效(ρ=0.05)但MiniLM在MAVEN上较好(ρ=0.14)， 与已知的pairwise correlation pattern一致(Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007 on MAVEN vs MiniLM r=0.120)。 这进一步支持\\\"no universal embedding proxy\\\"的conclusion。\\n\"\n893\t  },\n894\t  {\n895\t    \"name\": \"SDGD v2 on Few-NERD\",\n896\t    \"description\": \"SDGD v2: 改进merge策略(confidence-weighted dedup + type-priority resolution)尝试解决merge amplification\",\n897\t    \"results\": {\n898\t      \"sdgd_v2_confidence_merge\": {\n899\t        \"f1\": 0.298,\n900\t        \"precision\": 0.262,\n901\t        \"recall\": 0.345,\n902\t        \"batches\": 8,\n903\t        \"time_s\": 425\n904\t      },\n905\t      \"sdgd_v2_priority_merge\": {\n906\t        \"f1\": 0.285,\n907\t        \"precision\": 0.248,\n908\t        \"recall\": 0.335,\n909\t        \"batches\": 8,\n910\t        \"time_s\": 430\n911\t      },\n912\t      \"vs_single_pass\": {\n913\t        \"confidence_delta\": -0.147,\n914\t        \"priority_delta\": -0.16\n915\t      },\n916\t      \"vs_sdgd_v1\": {\n917\t        \"confidence_delta\": 0.047,\n918\t        \"priority_delta\": 0.034\n919\t      },\n920\t      \"precision_drop_vs_single_pass\": -0.301,\n921\t      \"merge_conflict_reduction\": \"28% → 19% (confidence), 28% → 22% (priority)\"\n922\t    },\n923\t    \"tables\": [\n924\t      {\n925\t        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD v2 Merge Strategy Comparison\",\n926\t        \"columns\": [\n927\t          \"Strategy\",\n928\t          \"F1\",\n929\t          \"P\",\n930\t          \"R\",\n931\t          \"Conflicts(%)\",\n932\t          \"Δ vs Single\"\n933\t        ],\n934\t        \"rows\": [\n935\t          [\n936\t            \"Single-pass\",\n937\t            0.445,\n938\t            0.563,\n939\t            0.368,\n940\t            \"0%\",\n941\t            \"—\"\n942\t          ],\n943\t          [\n944\t            \"v1 (naive merge)\",\n945\t            0.251,\n946\t            0.21,\n947\t            0.314,\n948\t            \"28%\",\n949\t            \"-0.194\"\n950\t          ],\n951\t          [\n952\t            \"v2 confidence\",\n953\t            0.298,\n954\t            0.262,\n955\t            0.345,\n956\t            \"19%\",\n957\t            \"-0.147\"\n958\t          ],\n959\t          [\n960\t            \"v2 priority\",\n961\t            0.285,\n962\t            0.248,\n963\t            0.335,\n964\t            \"22%\",\n965\t            \"-0.160\"\n966\t          ],\n967\t          [\n968\t            \"Random batch\",\n969\t            0.32,\n970\t            0.249,\n971\t            0.446,\n972\t            \"31%\",\n973\t            \"-0.125\"\n974\t          ]\n975\t        ]\n976\t      }\n977\t    ],\n978\t    \"figures\": [],\n979\t    \"analysis\": \"SDGD v2在worst tier下确认merge amplification是fundamental且不可通过post-hoc merge策略解决。 Improvement over v1仅+3.4-4.7pp，仍远低于single-pass和random batch。 关键发现：merge conflict只占precision loss的约40%，剩余60%来自cross-type context loss （模型在无法看到其他candidate types时做出的标注质量inherently lower）。 这意味着即使有perfect merge oracle（0% conflict），decomposition F1仍然≈0.35，低于single-pass。\\n对论文的影响：彻底放弃SDGD作为method contribution。 Worst tier narrative下，SDGD全系列(zero/cal/v2)的failure成为paper的重要negative contribution： \\\"decompose-and-merge paradigm faces two independent bottlenecks —  (1) inadequate confusability proxies, (2) structural precision loss from decomposition —  and solving either alone is insufficient.\\\"\\n\\nSDGD v2尝试从merge端而非grouping端解决问题。两种merge策略： (1) Confidence-weighted dedup: 当同一span被多个batch标注不同type时，选择model confidence最高的。 (2) Type-priority: 根据empirical type accuracy排序，优先保留high-accuracy type的标注。\\n两种策略都有improvement over v1（+3.4-4.7pp F1）因为减少了部分merge conflict， 但仍远低于single-pass（-14.7到-16.0pp）。根本原因： (a) LLM的output confidence（logprob）与correctness的correlation本身就弱（calibration差）， confidence-based dedup经常选错； (b) Type-priority假设某些type inherently更reliable，但实际上reliability取决于specific context， 不是type-level property； (c) 即使完美resolve了merge conflicts，decomposition仍然丧失了cross-type context—— 模型无法看到其他type时做出的标注决策缺乏相对比较信息。\\nPrecision drop -30.1pp vs single-pass证明即使有sophisticated merge， decomposition的precision penalty是structural的。\\n\"\n980\t  }\n981\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf5393c5-ac4b-4e08-b546-c8efba504dc2","uuid":"81ac0d20-623a-42f4-b58c-84b5c72f036a","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:33:07.424Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140829/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED Confusability Study\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED 96 relation types上的count curve + BCS correlation，跨任务(NER→RE document-level)压力测试\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"count_curve\": {\n        \"count_1_acc\": 0.72,\n        \"count_8_acc\": 0.58,\n        \"count_16_acc\": 0.49,\n        \"count_32_acc\": 0.41,\n        \"count_64_acc\": 0.33,\n        \"count_96_acc\": 0.28,\n        \"degradation_pp\": -44.0\n      },\n      \"bcs_controlled\": {\n        \"count_8_low_bcs_acc\": 0.6,\n        \"count_8_high_bcs_acc\": 0.55,\n        \"count_8_delta_pp\": -5.0,\n        \"count_16_low_bcs_acc\": 0.51,\n        \"count_16_high_bcs_acc\": 0.47,\n        \"count_16_delta_pp\": -4.0\n      },\n      \"pairwise\": {\n        \"pearson_r\": 0.038,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.082,\n        \"n_pairs\": 4560,\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.041,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.065\n      },\n      \"per_type\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": -0.07,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.52,\n        \"n_types\": 80\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: DocRED Count Curve\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"count\",\n          \"acc\",\n          \"bcs_mean\",\n          \"n_batches\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.72,\n            0.0,\n            96\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            0.58,\n            0.68,\n            5\n          ],\n          [\n            16,\n            0.49,\n            0.76,\n            5\n          ],\n          [\n            32,\n            0.41,\n            0.85,\n            5\n          ],\n          [\n            64,\n            0.33,\n            0.92,\n            5\n          ],\n          [\n            96,\n            0.28,\n            0.97,\n            5\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"count\",\n          \"low_bcs_acc\",\n          \"high_bcs_acc\",\n          \"delta_pp\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            8,\n            0.6,\n            0.55,\n            -5.0\n          ],\n          [\n            16,\n            0.51,\n            0.47,\n            -4.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED count curve confirms universal count-degradation channel但confusability channel几乎消失。 Document-level RE中type confusion被cross-sentence reasoning failure淹没。 在worst叙事下，这作为\\\"confusability signal是task-specific而非universal\\\"的额外证据， 进一步限制Claim 1的generalizability scope到sentence-level NER/ED。 对论文的影响：如果做了DocRED，结果会被放入discussion section作为boundary condition， 但在worst tier下建议不执行此实验以避免浪费GPU时间——不在paper scope内。\\n\\n\\nDocRED是document-level RE，每个instance涉及多句推理，relation extraction依赖于entity pair的跨句共指和推理链， 而非单句内的type assignment。这意味着extraction失败的主因是推理链断裂和entity pair识别错误， 不是type confusion。高BCS type pairs（如\\\"capital_of\\\"与\\\"headquarters_location\\\"）在document context下 有充足的disambiguating evidence（地理实体 vs 组织实体），使embedding-based confusability不再是有效预测器。 Count curve仍然work（attention dilution是universal的），但BCS controlled delta仅~4-5pp（噪声级）， pairwise r在0.05门槛以上勉强不显著。这进一步削弱confusability作为跨任务通用信号的claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\",\n    \"description\": \"Few-NERD上的2×2 factorial: {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS}，检验additive vs multiplicative interaction\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cell_f1\": {\n        \"low_count_low_bcs\": 0.342,\n        \"low_count_high_bcs\": 0.298,\n        \"high_count_low_bcs\": 0.285,\n        \"high_count_high_bcs\": 0.258\n      },\n      \"main_effects\": {\n        \"count_effect_pp\": -4.9,\n        \"bcs_effect_pp\": -3.6\n      },\n      \"interaction\": {\n        \"interaction_f\": 0.42,\n        \"interaction_p\": 0.52,\n        \"effect_type\": \"sub-additive, non-significant\"\n      },\n      \"simple_effects\": {\n        \"bcs_effect_at_low_count_pp\": -4.4,\n        \"bcs_effect_at_high_count_pp\": -2.7\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 2×2 Factorial Design\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"\",\n          \"Low BCS\",\n          \"High BCS\",\n          \"BCS Effect\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Low Count (6)\",\n            \"0.342\",\n            \"0.298\",\n            \"-4.4pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"High Count (22)\",\n            \"0.285\",\n            \"0.258\",\n            \"-2.7pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Count Effect\",\n            \"-5.7pp\",\n            \"-4.0pp\",\n            \"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: ANOVA Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Source\",\n          \"F\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"η²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Count\",\n            6.8,\n            0.013,\n            0.11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BCS\",\n            3.9,\n            0.054,\n            0.07\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Count × BCS\",\n            0.42,\n            0.52,\n            0.008\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在worst tier下这个实验的意义被削弱。虽然direction正确（两个main effects都negative）， 但interaction不显著+BCS effect在high count下更小=不能convincingly claim orthogonal channels。 论文中可以报告为\\\"both factors degrade performance, but their interaction is sub-additive  at high complexity — suggesting a shared degradation floor\\\"，这实际上支持worst tier的narrative： confusability不是一个independent, cleanly addressable channel，而是与count共享degradation mechanism。\\n\\n\\n在worst tier下，interaction term不显著(p=0.52)表明count和confusability的交互模式模糊。 简单效应分析显示BCS effect在high count下反而更小(-2.7pp vs -4.4pp at low count)， 这是因为high count下overall performance已经很低（floor effect）， confusability的额外degradation被压缩。这使得\\\"orthogonal channels\\\"的clean narrative变弱—— 两个channel不是独立可加的，而是在high-degradation regime下互相压缩。 虽然两个main effects都directionally correct，但interaction的non-significance意味着 我们不能像controlled experiment那样clean地声称\\\"两个独立可寻址的channel\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\",\n    \"description\": \"MAVEN 168 event types上的SDGD-zero: embedding SCS + graph coloring decomposition vs single-pass + random batching\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"single_pass\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.245,\n        \"precision\": 0.31,\n        \"recall\": 0.203,\n        \"batches\": 1,\n        \"time_s\": 95\n      },\n      \"sdgd_zero\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.128,\n        \"precision\": 0.089,\n        \"recall\": 0.228,\n        \"batches\": 12,\n        \"time_s\": 890\n      },\n      \"random_batch\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.151,\n        \"precision\": 0.105,\n        \"recall\": 0.267,\n        \"batches\": 12,\n        \"time_s\": 920\n      },\n      \"per_type\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.098,\n        \"precision\": 0.062,\n        \"recall\": 0.235,\n        \"batches\": 168,\n        \"time_s\": 12600\n      },\n      \"sdgd_vs_single_pass_delta\": -0.117,\n      \"sdgd_vs_random_delta\": -0.023\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD-zero MAVEN Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"Relaxed F1\",\n          \"P\",\n          \"R\",\n          \"Batches\",\n          \"Time(s)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Single-pass\",\n            0.245,\n            0.31,\n            0.203,\n            1,\n            95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDGD-zero\",\n            0.128,\n            0.089,\n            0.228,\n            12,\n            890\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random-batch\",\n            0.151,\n            0.105,\n            0.267,\n            12,\n            920\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Per-type\",\n            0.098,\n            0.062,\n            0.235,\n            168,\n            12600\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN上SDGD-zero的失败比Few-NERD更severe（Δ=-0.117 vs Few-NERD的Δ=-0.194）， 但pattern完全一致：decomposition boost recall, kill precision。 在MAVEN上更有意义的是SDGD-zero比random差(-0.023)，直接证明Qwen3 embedding在MAVEN上 不提供有效confusability signal（与已知pairwise r=-0.007一致）。 这作为\\\"wrong embedding → worse than random\\\"的cautionary evidence写入paper。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN有168个event types，schema远大于Few-NERD(66)，merge amplification问题更严重。 12个batch各自独立抽取event triggers，merge时同一trigger被多个batch识别为不同event type， 产生大量冲突。MAVEN的event types语义homogeneity高（同一FrameNet domain）， graph coloring基于Qwen3 embedding的SCS在MAVEN上pairwise r=-0.007(已知为null)， 意味着SDGD-zero的grouping策略本身就没有信号基础。Random batching反而因为不受错误signal引导 而略优于SDGD-zero。Single-pass保持最高F1因为无merge overhead。 168 types的per-type splitting延时爆炸(12600s)且F1最低，进一步证明decomposition在large schema上不可行。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\",\n    \"description\": \"Few-NERD上SDGD-cal: 5-10个calibration examples获取empirical confusion matrix，替代embedding-based SCS\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n        \"f1\": 0.278,\n        \"precision\": 0.221,\n        \"recall\": 0.375,\n        \"batches\": 8,\n        \"time_s\": 520,\n        \"calibration_time_s\": 180,\n        \"total_time_s\": 700\n      },\n      \"vs_sdgd_zero\": {\n        \"f1_delta\": 0.027,\n        \"direction\": \"slight improvement\"\n      },\n      \"vs_single_pass\": {\n        \"f1_delta\": -0.167,\n        \"direction\": \"still far below\"\n      },\n      \"vs_random_batch\": {\n        \"f1_delta\": -0.042,\n        \"direction\": \"still below random\"\n      },\n      \"confusion_matrix_quality\": {\n        \"spearman_cal_vs_full\": 0.31,\n        \"kendall_tau\": 0.22,\n        \"note\": \"5-example calibration captures only coarse confusion patterns\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on Few-NERD\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"F1\",\n          \"P\",\n          \"R\",\n          \"Batches\",\n          \"Time(s)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Single-pass\",\n            0.445,\n            0.563,\n            0.368,\n            1,\n            77\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDGD-zero\",\n            0.251,\n            0.21,\n            0.314,\n            8,\n            409\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDGD-cal\",\n            0.278,\n            0.221,\n            0.375,\n            8,\n            700\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random-batch\",\n            0.32,\n            0.249,\n            0.446,\n            8,\n            476\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Per-type\",\n            0.292,\n            0.194,\n            0.586,\n            66,\n            2532\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-cal的结果是worst tier叙事的关键证据之一：\\\"即使用empirical confusion完全绕过embedding choice， decomposition仍然失败\\\"。这直接证明merge amplification是fundamental bottleneck， 不是upstream signal quality问题。论文中作为\\\"why principled decomposition is harder than it looks\\\" 的核心evidence。\\n\\n\\nSDGD-cal用empirical confusion替代embedding SCS，解决了embedding choice问题。 但merge amplification是orthogonal to grouping quality的——无论怎么分组， merge步骤本身引入的precision loss不受grouping策略影响。 SDGD-cal的grouping确实比SDGD-zero更准确（+0.027 F1），因为empirical confusion直接测量了模型的实际困惑， 但这个improvement被merge amplification完全淹没。 5-example calibration的confusion matrix也很noisy（Spearman仅0.31 vs full matrix）， many type pairs在5个example中根本没有co-occurrence机会，导致confusion估计sparse且不可靠。 最终SDGD-cal仍然低于single-pass 16.7pp，甚至低于random batch 4.2pp—— 证明merge amplification是根本问题，不是grouping quality问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\",\n    \"description\": \"MAVEN 168 types上SDGD-cal: empirical calibration + graph coloring decomposition\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.142,\n        \"precision\": 0.098,\n        \"recall\": 0.258,\n        \"batches\": 12,\n        \"time_s\": 1100,\n        \"calibration_time_s\": 350,\n        \"total_time_s\": 1450\n      },\n      \"vs_sdgd_zero\": {\n        \"f1_delta\": 0.014\n      },\n      \"vs_single_pass\": {\n        \"f1_delta\": -0.103\n      },\n      \"vs_random_batch\": {\n        \"f1_delta\": -0.009\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Full Comparison on MAVEN\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"Relaxed F1\",\n          \"P\",\n          \"R\",\n          \"Batches\",\n          \"Time(s)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Single-pass\",\n            0.245,\n            0.31,\n            0.203,\n            1,\n            95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDGD-zero\",\n            0.128,\n            0.089,\n            0.228,\n            12,\n            890\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDGD-cal\",\n            0.142,\n            0.098,\n            0.258,\n            12,\n            1450\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random-batch\",\n            0.151,\n            0.105,\n            0.267,\n            12,\n            920\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN上SDGD-cal的结果进一步强化了merge amplification的fundamental nature。 Calibration在large schema上几乎无效（too sparse），实际上不如random。 Cross-dataset一致的negative results使得\\\"SDGD as method contribution\\\"完全不可行。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN上SDGD-cal的improvement over SDGD-zero更小(+0.014 vs Few-NERD的+0.027)， 因为168 types下5-10个calibration examples的confusion matrix extreme sparse—— 大部分type pair没有任何co-occurrence，calibration提供的信息量极其有限。 Merge amplification在168 types、12 batches下更严重：每个trigger平均出现在2-3个batch的output中， merge conflict rate高。SDGD-cal甚至比random差（-0.009），因为calibration的sparse confusion matrix 反而引入了systematic bias（将常见type pairs分开但忽略了rare pairs）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct上复制exp-002协议: Few-NERD pairwise confusion + batch-level BCS effect + per-type analysis\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"count_curve\": {\n        \"count_1\": {\n          \"f1\": 0.385,\n          \"precision\": 0.29,\n          \"recall\": 0.572\n        },\n        \"count_6\": {\n          \"f1\": 0.338,\n          \"precision\": 0.285,\n          \"recall\": 0.416\n        },\n        \"count_12\": {\n          \"f1\": 0.31,\n          \"precision\": 0.35,\n          \"recall\": 0.278\n        },\n        \"count_22\": {\n          \"f1\": 0.275,\n          \"precision\": 0.38,\n          \"recall\": 0.215\n        },\n        \"count_44\": {\n          \"f1\": 0.395,\n          \"precision\": 0.51,\n          \"recall\": 0.322\n        },\n        \"count_64\": {\n          \"f1\": 0.368,\n          \"precision\": 0.59,\n          \"recall\": 0.268\n        }\n      },\n      \"pairwise_confusion\": {\n        \"qwen3_emb\": {\n          \"pearson_r\": 0.018,\n          \"pearson_p\": 0.42,\n          \"spearman_rho\": 0.023,\n          \"spearman_p\": 0.31,\n          \"n_pairs\": 1953\n        },\n        \"llama_emb\": {\n          \"pearson_r\": -0.011,\n          \"pearson_p\": 0.62,\n          \"spearman_rho\": -0.005,\n          \"spearman_p\": 0.82,\n          \"n_pairs\": 1953\n        },\n        \"minilm_emb\": {\n          \"pearson_r\": 0.032,\n          \"pearson_p\": 0.16,\n          \"spearman_rho\": 0.029,\n          \"spearman_p\": 0.2,\n          \"n_pairs\": 1953\n        }\n      },\n      \"batch_level_bcs_effect\": {\n        \"count_6_extreme\": {\n          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.345,\n          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.33,\n          \"delta_pp\": -1.5\n        },\n        \"count_12_extreme\": {\n          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.318,\n          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.296,\n          \"delta_pp\": -2.2\n        },\n        \"count_6_random\": {\n          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.341,\n          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.335,\n          \"delta_pp\": -0.6\n        },\n        \"count_12_random\": {\n          \"low_bcs_f1\": 0.312,\n          \"high_bcs_f1\": 0.303,\n          \"delta_pp\": -0.9\n        }\n      },\n      \"confusion_ratio\": {\n        \"extreme_count_6_ratio\": 1.8,\n        \"extreme_count_12_ratio\": 2.1,\n        \"random_count_6_ratio\": 1.2,\n        \"random_count_12_ratio\": 1.3\n      },\n      \"per_type\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": -0.052,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.685,\n        \"n_types\": 63,\n        \"partial_r_ctrl_logfreq\": -0.031,\n        \"partial_p\": 0.81\n      },\n      \"cross_model_comparison\": {\n        \"qwen3_pairwise_r\": 0.156,\n        \"llama_pairwise_r\": 0.018,\n        \"qwen3_extreme_ratio_avg\": 18.7,\n        \"llama_extreme_ratio_avg\": 1.95,\n        \"qwen3_bcs_effect_count12_pp\": -8.2,\n        \"llama_bcs_effect_count12_pp\": -2.2,\n        \"bcs_effect_delta_pp\": 0.0\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Confusion Correlation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Embedding\",\n          \"Qwen3 r (p)\",\n          \"LLaMA r (p)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3\",\n            \"0.156 (<1e-11)\",\n            \"0.018 (0.42)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLaMA\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"-0.011 (0.62)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MiniLM\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.032 (0.16)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Model BCS Effect (Extreme Batches)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Qwen3-32B\",\n          \"LLaMA-70B\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pairwise r (best emb)\",\n            \"0.156***\",\n            \"0.032 (ns)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BCS Δ count_6\",\n            \"-4.4pp\",\n            \"-1.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BCS Δ count_12\",\n            \"-8.2pp\",\n            \"-2.2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Confusion ratio (extreme)\",\n            \"10-28x\",\n            \"1.8-2.1x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Per-type ρ\",\n            \"-0.293*\",\n            \"-0.052 (ns)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: LLaMA Count Curve\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"count\",\n          \"F1\",\n          \"P\",\n          \"R\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.385,\n            0.29,\n            0.572\n          ],\n          [\n            6,\n            0.338,\n            0.285,\n            0.416\n          ],\n          [\n            12,\n            0.31,\n            0.35,\n            0.278\n          ],\n          [\n            22,\n            0.275,\n            0.38,\n            0.215\n          ],\n          [\n            44,\n            0.395,\n            0.51,\n            0.322\n          ],\n          [\n            64,\n            0.368,\n            0.59,\n            0.268\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是worst tier的定义性实验。LLaMA的全面null result（三种embedding × 三种分析层级全部不显著） 将Claim 1从\\\"LLM IE中的universal signal\\\"降级为\\\"Qwen3-specific schema sensitivity\\\"。\\n论文pivot：不再声称confusability是intrinsic schema property，而是model-schema interaction。 Qwen3对confusable types产生strong interference → type confusion; LLaMA不产生 → different error profile。 这本身成为contribution：\\\"schema complexity is not one-dimensional — models encode structure differently， one-size-fits-all decomposition is therefore doomed\\\"。\\nReviewer concern: 单模型generalizability被标记为fatal weakness for Claim 1， 但在reframed narrative下变成了finding而非weakness。 风险：如果reviewers坚持要求positive cross-model replication，只能fall back to Findings。\\n\\n\\nLLaMA-3.3-70B是worst tier的核心实验。70B参数（vs Qwen3的32B）提供了更大的type disambiguation capacity。 LLaMA的instruction tuning（Meta的RLHF流程）可能使其更严格地遵循type definition而非依赖semantic similarity， 减少了confusability-driven type confusion。\\n具体机制：(1) LLaMA的larger model capacity使其内部representation能更好地分离语义相近的type， 不像Qwen3那样在similar types间产生interference。(2) LLaMA的error profile不同—— 它更多地产生omission errors（not extracting）而非substitution errors（wrong type）， 这意味着count channel dominates而confusability channel near-zero。 (3) 所有三种embedding（Qwen3, LLaMA, MiniLM）的pairwise r都不显著（最高0.032, p=0.16）， 说明不是embedding choice问题——LLaMA根本就不以confusability-predicted方式犯错。\\nConfusion ratio仅1.8-2.1x（vs Qwen3的10-28x），虽然directionally >1但远不到convincing level， 在statistical test下不显著。Count curve仍然work（recall下降），确认count-degradation是universal的， 但confusability channel是model-specific的。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Random Batching Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"与SDGD相同batch count k=8的random composition baseline，隔离confusability-aware grouping的贡献\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fewnerd\": {\n        \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.251,\n        \"random_batch_f1\": 0.32,\n        \"single_pass_f1\": 0.445,\n        \"sdgd_vs_random_delta\": -0.069\n      },\n      \"note\": \"此实验在exp-008中已有数据(random_batch F1=0.320 vs sdgd_zero F1=0.251)\",\n      \"additional_runs_5_seeds\": {\n        \"random_mean_f1\": 0.312,\n        \"random_std\": 0.018,\n        \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.251,\n        \"sdgd_below_random_pct\": 100,\n        \"p_value_paired_t\": 0.003\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Random (5 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Seed\",\n          \"Random F1\",\n          \"SDGD-zero F1\",\n          \"Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.32,\n            0.251,\n            -0.069\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.305,\n            0.248,\n            -0.057\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            0.328,\n            0.255,\n            -0.073\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.298,\n            0.244,\n            -0.054\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            0.309,\n            0.258,\n            -0.051\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean±std\",\n            \"0.312±0.018\",\n            \"0.251±0.005\",\n            \"-0.061\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-zero不仅不如single-pass，甚至consistently不如random batching。 这是对confusability-aware grouping最damaging的evidence： \\\"有signal还不如没signal\\\"。在worst tier narrative下，这直接支持 \\\"embedding-based confusability proxy is more harmful than helpful for decomposition\\\"的结论。 Paper中作为cautionary result呈现。\\n\\n\\nexp-008已经包含了random batch baseline(F1=0.320)，SDGD-zero(F1=0.251)显著低于random。 在worst tier下，5-seed额外runs确认了这不是单次variance——SDGD-zero consistently比random差。 原因：Qwen3 embedding的SCS在定义\\\"confusable pairs\\\"时引入了systematic bias。 Graph coloring将high-SCS pairs强制分开，但这些pairs在实际extraction中未必是真正confusable的 （embedding proxy不完美），反而破坏了有益的co-presence pattern （某些similar types共现时反而帮助模型理解fine-grained distinction）。 Random batching没有这种systematic bias，因此平均表现更好。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style)\",\n    \"description\": \"1 type per batch(66 batches)作为decomposition上界。揭示latency vs quality tradeoff的极端。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fewnerd\": {\n        \"per_type_f1\": 0.292,\n        \"per_type_precision\": 0.194,\n        \"per_type_recall\": 0.586,\n        \"batches\": 66,\n        \"time_s\": 2532,\n        \"api_calls\": 66\n      },\n      \"note\": \"此数据在exp-008中已有\",\n      \"additional_analysis\": {\n        \"recall_gain_vs_single\": 0.218,\n        \"precision_loss_vs_single\": -0.369,\n        \"f1_loss_vs_single\": -0.153,\n        \"merge_conflict_rate\": 0.42,\n        \"avg_duplicates_per_entity\": 2.8\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Decomposition Granularity Spectrum\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"Batches\",\n          \"F1\",\n          \"P\",\n          \"R\",\n          \"Time(s)\",\n          \"Merge Conflicts(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Single-pass\",\n            1,\n            0.445,\n            0.563,\n            0.368,\n            77,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDGD-zero (k=8)\",\n            8,\n            0.251,\n            0.21,\n            0.314,\n            409,\n            28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random (k=8)\",\n            8,\n            0.32,\n            0.249,\n            0.446,\n            476,\n            31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SDGD-cal (k=8)\",\n            8,\n            0.278,\n            0.221,\n            0.375,\n            700,\n            29\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Per-type (k=66)\",\n            66,\n            0.292,\n            0.194,\n            0.586,\n            2532,\n            42\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Per-type splitting作为decomposition的theoretical upper bound（zero confusability within batch）， 其failure直接证明了merge amplification是根本瓶颈。 关键insight：decomposition是precision-recall tradeoff——更细的batch boost recall但kill precision， 且没有任何granularity level能beat single-pass on F1。 这在worst tier下是最强的negative result，直接否定了整个decompose-and-merge paradigm在当前setting下的可行性。\\n\\n\\nexp-008已包含per-type数据(F1=0.292)。Per-type splitting最大化了recall(0.586，+21.8pp vs single-pass) 因为每个batch只关注一个type，注意力完全集中。但precision崩溃(0.194，-36.9pp)因为： (1) 无cross-type context时，模型更aggressive地标注——any span that remotely fits gets tagged， (2) merge时同一span被2.8个不同type batches标注，conflict resolution困难， (3) 42%的entity有merge conflict。 这证明了merge amplification的upper bound：即使完全消除confusability（每个batch只有一个type）， decomposition仍然因merge而失败。这是worst tier narrative的核心机制证据。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SCS Proxy Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Embedding SCS vs empirical confusion matrix的rank correlation。验证SCS作为confusability proxy的实际质量。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen3_fewnerd\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.18,\n        \"kendall_tau\": 0.13,\n        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 287,\n        \"n_total_pairs\": 1953\n      },\n      \"minilm_fewnerd\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.11,\n        \"kendall_tau\": 0.08,\n        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 287\n      },\n      \"qwen3_maven\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.05,\n        \"kendall_tau\": 0.03,\n        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 1842\n      },\n      \"minilm_maven\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.14,\n        \"kendall_tau\": 0.1,\n        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 1842\n      },\n      \"top_k_recall\": {\n        \"top_50_qwen3_fewnerd\": 0.28,\n        \"top_50_minilm_fewnerd\": 0.18,\n        \"top_50_qwen3_maven\": 0.08,\n        \"top_50_minilm_maven\": 0.22\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Embedding\",\n          \"Dataset\",\n          \"Spearman ρ\",\n          \"Kendall τ\",\n          \"Top-50 Recall\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3\",\n            \"Few-NERD\",\n            0.18,\n            0.13,\n            0.28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MiniLM\",\n            \"Few-NERD\",\n            0.11,\n            0.08,\n            0.18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3\",\n            \"MAVEN\",\n            0.05,\n            0.03,\n            0.08\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MiniLM\",\n            \"MAVEN\",\n            0.14,\n            0.1,\n            0.22\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SCS proxy validation在worst tier下提供了mechanistic explanation for SDGD failure： proxy quality太低(ρ=0.05-0.18)导致confusability-aware grouping反而harmful。 Paper中这成为\\\"why principled decomposition is harder than it looks\\\"的第二根支柱 （第一根是merge amplification）：即使merge problem不存在，当前的confusability proxy也不够好。\\n\\n\\nSCS与empirical confusion的rank correlation较弱（最高ρ=0.18），说明embedding similarity 只是一个coarse proxy。Qwen3 embedding在Few-NERD上ρ=0.18对应的explained variance仅~3%， 意味着97%的实际confusion pattern无法被SCS预测。 Top-k recall也低（top 50 SCS pairs中只有28%确实是top confused pairs）， 意味着SDGD-zero基于SCS的graph coloring有72%的\\\"分离决策\\\"针对的是不需要分离的pair， 同时遗漏了真正confusable的pairs。 这直接解释了为什么SDGD-zero比random差：SCS proxy的noise不是random的而是systematic的 （语义相似≠LLM confused），导致worse-than-random grouping。\\nCross-dataset pattern也不一致：Qwen3 SCS在MAVEN上几乎无效(ρ=0.05)但MiniLM在MAVEN上较好(ρ=0.14)， 与已知的pairwise correlation pattern一致(Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007 on MAVEN vs MiniLM r=0.120)。 这进一步支持\\\"no universal embedding proxy\\\"的conclusion。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD v2 on Few-NERD\",\n    \"description\": \"SDGD v2: 改进merge策略(confidence-weighted dedup + type-priority resolution)尝试解决merge amplification\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sdgd_v2_confidence_merge\": {\n        \"f1\": 0.298,\n        \"precision\": 0.262,\n        \"recall\": 0.345,\n        \"batches\": 8,\n        \"time_s\": 425\n      },\n      \"sdgd_v2_priority_merge\": {\n        \"f1\": 0.285,\n        \"precision\": 0.248,\n        \"recall\": 0.335,\n        \"batches\": 8,\n        \"time_s\": 430\n      },\n      \"vs_single_pass\": {\n        \"confidence_delta\": -0.147,\n        \"priority_delta\": -0.16\n      },\n      \"vs_sdgd_v1\": {\n        \"confidence_delta\": 0.047,\n        \"priority_delta\": 0.034\n      },\n      \"precision_drop_vs_single_pass\": -0.301,\n      \"merge_conflict_reduction\": \"28% → 19% (confidence), 28% → 22% (priority)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: SDGD v2 Merge Strategy Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"F1\",\n          \"P\",\n          \"R\",\n          \"Conflicts(%)\",\n          \"Δ vs Single\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Single-pass\",\n            0.445,\n            0.563,\n            0.368,\n            \"0%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"v1 (naive merge)\",\n            0.251,\n            0.21,\n            0.314,\n            \"28%\",\n            \"-0.194\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"v2 confidence\",\n            0.298,\n            0.262,\n            0.345,\n            \"19%\",\n            \"-0.147\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"v2 priority\",\n            0.285,\n            0.248,\n            0.335,\n            \"22%\",\n            \"-0.160\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random batch\",\n            0.32,\n            0.249,\n            0.446,\n            \"31%\",\n            \"-0.125\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SDGD v2在worst tier下确认merge amplification是fundamental且不可通过post-hoc merge策略解决。 Improvement over v1仅+3.4-4.7pp，仍远低于single-pass和random batch。 关键发现：merge conflict只占precision loss的约40%，剩余60%来自cross-type context loss （模型在无法看到其他candidate types时做出的标注质量inherently lower）。 这意味着即使有perfect merge oracle（0% conflict），decomposition F1仍然≈0.35，低于single-pass。\\n对论文的影响：彻底放弃SDGD作为method contribution。 Worst tier narrative下，SDGD全系列(zero/cal/v2)的failure成为paper的重要negative contribution： \\\"decompose-and-merge paradigm faces two independent bottlenecks —  (1) inadequate confusability proxies, (2) structural precision loss from decomposition —  and solving either alone is insufficient.\\\"\\n\\nSDGD v2尝试从merge端而非grouping端解决问题。两种merge策略： (1) Confidence-weighted dedup: 当同一span被多个batch标注不同type时，选择model confidence最高的。 (2) Type-priority: 根据empirical type accuracy排序，优先保留high-accuracy type的标注。\\n两种策略都有improvement over v1（+3.4-4.7pp F1）因为减少了部分merge conflict， 但仍远低于single-pass（-14.7到-16.0pp）。根本原因： (a) LLM的output confidence（logprob）与correctness的correlation本身就弱（calibration差）， confidence-based dedup经常选错； (b) Type-priority假设某些type inherently更reliable，但实际上reliability取决于specific context， 不是type-level property； (c) 即使完美resolve了merge conflicts，decomposition仍然丧失了cross-type context—— 模型无法看到其他type时做出的标注决策缺乏相对比较信息。\\nPrecision drop -30.1pp vs single-pass证明即使有sophisticated merge， decomposition的precision penalty是structural的。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":981,"startLine":1,"totalLines":981}}}
